4. Street basemap tiles — fetched at runtime, never redistributed
-----------------------------------------------------------------
   The Map tab can draw a street basemap under the boundaries. The tiles are
   requested from the provider's servers while the page is open and are not
   stored in this repository or in the built HTML:

   - CARTO "Positron" and "Dark Matter" basemaps (the default):
     map data © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database
     Licence (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright); cartography © CARTO
     (https://carto.com/attributions), served under CARTO's basemap terms.
   - OpenStreetMap standard tiles: © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL;
     served subject to the OpenStreetMap Foundation tile usage policy
     (https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/tiles/).

   Each tile request is an ordinary web request to the provider's servers. It
   carries the viewer's IP address, browser identification and request headers
   together with the tile coordinates (the area and zoom level on screen), and
   is handled under the provider's privacy policy. Nothing else is sent.

   The atlas shows the required attribution in the map's corner. Selecting
   "None" under Basemap stops all tile requests; nothing else in the atlas
   uses the network.


